<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia employment fell 40,300 in May.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia employment fell 40,300 in May.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's seasonally adjusted estimate of the number of employed persons fell 40,300 in May to 8.380 million, against 8.421 million in April and 8.328 million a year earlier, the Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate rose to 8.8 percent from 8.7 percent in April, compared with 8.5 percent in May 1996. Full-time employment fell around 23,100, while part-time fell 17,200.</p>
<p>Economists had on average expected employment to rise around 15,000 in May, with the unemployment rate staying steady at 8.7 percent.  </p>
<p>AUSTRALIAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>    (Seasonally adj)	May  97    April 97	May  96</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.8 pct     8.7 pct	8.5 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.38 million    8.42 million     8.33 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed		809,800     802,300	774,600</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.2 pct    63.5 pct     63.6 pct</p>
<p>(Unadjusted)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.6 pct     8.7 pct	8.3 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.39 million    8.41 million     8.34 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed		791,900     799,600	758,200</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.1 pct    63.4 pct     63.5 pct</p>
<p>(Trend Estimates)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate    8.8 pct	8.8 pct	8.5 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		8.40 million     8.40 million     8.32 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed	     809,200	806,000	777,300</p>
<p>    Participation Rate  63.3 pct     63.4 pct     63.5 pct</p>
